en:
"Keep you company...?
You mean you'll come with us to check on Hanako-san, sir?"
That was Hosoda.{p}

Our only light was the dim glow of a single flashlight.
The teacher took the lead and started walking, lighting the floor at our feet.
And as he slowly walked, he began to talk, a little at a time.{p}

On the other side of this wall, there was a staircase.
A staircase leading underground.
The old school building is made of wood, but that staircase and the basement beyond it were made of stone.{p}

And right then, that story about the shelter flashed through my head.
Before I knew it, I'd broken into a run.
I was really scared.{p}

My class had no choice but to go down that hallway.
Honestly, I hated the idea.
But what could I do?{p}

...Please don't let anything happen.
...Please, please don't let anything happen.
And just as I thought I must be past the wall by now...{p}

"Aaaaaaaaaaaaah!"
I screamed at the top of my lungs.
The instant I screamed, the skeleton soldiers who'd been marching so proudly collapsed one after another, like puppets with their strings cut.{p}

When I heard my own scream, I was crouched down in the schoolyard.
My classmates had formed a circle around me, keeping their distance.
They were looking at me like I was something creepy, whispering among themselves.{p}

Well, Kazama was the only one who told some story that made no sense at all, but I'll put up with that.
Tomorrow I can just ask Hino why he invited Kazama of all people{f:|}.
It had set my heart pounding, but it was an interesting experience{f:|}.{p}

{f:I|I} sighed and put down the receiver.
{f:I|I} really was a pushover{f:.|.}
Who'd have thought I'd get called out to school at this hour, and actually {f:agree|agree} to it?
And on a day like this, of all days...{p}

Had {f:my|my} nerves gone numb{f:?|?}
Normally I'd be scared out of my wits{f:,|,} wouldn't I?
Or had hearing all those scary stories {f:made|made} me lose it{f:?|?}
Thinking about all that, {f:I|I} headed for school.{p}

At midnight, the old school building was as eerie as if a devil lived there{f:.|.}
Hosoda had come well prepared; he'd even brought a flashlight.
The flashlight lit up the grimy wall.
"...It was around here, I think. ...There it is!"{p}

The power saw switched on, and the motor's whine, like a woman's shriek, blew the silence apart.
"Hyahhahha!"
Hosoda raised it high and slashed into the wall without a moment's hesitation.{p}

With a furious grinding, the wall crumbled away easily.
Without the slightest resistance, the wall laid its innards bare.
...It was too dark to see well.{p}

"No... I'll pass."
{f:I|I} shook my head.
He might be understanding, but he was still a teacher{f:.|.}
Scolding {f:us|us} was one thing, but actually joining in with us?
Wasn't he getting a little too carried away{f:?|?}
Besides, I had a bad feeling about this{f:.|.}
So much had already happened today{f:.|.}
It was more than enough for one day's worth of experience, {f:wasn't it|wasn't it}?
I'd had enough{f:.|.}
"{f:Sorry|Sorry}... {f:We're|We're} going home now."{p}

Once I got home, that premonition grew more and more certain.
Something bad was going to happen.
Something evil was lurking in that school.
{f:I told myself it was ridiculous.|Maybe I was being ridiculous.}
A lot had happened today{f:.|.}
That was why my nerves were on edge{f:.|.}
But even telling myself that, the unease wouldn't go away.
What was wrong with me{f:?|?}{p}

...The school was just as usual, almost disappointingly so.
No students making a fuss, no police cars.
Seeing that, {f:I|I} felt a little embarrassed.
What had I expected to happen{f:?|?}
I felt as if I'd only just woken from a long, long dream.
Yesterday must have shocked me more than I'd realized{f:.|.}
That was why I'd made such a fuss over {f:nothing|nothing}.
I had to apologize to Hosoda and the others.{p}

...In the end, Hosoda never came.
Now I couldn't stop wondering about Mr. Kuroki.
After school, {f:I|I} worked up my nerve and went looking for my homeroom teacher.{p}

"Maybe you have a strong sixth sense, {a}.
You've found out something an ordinary student wouldn't notice.
Take my advice and forget it."{p}

What was the teacher {f:saying|saying}?
Forget it?
When Hosoda might have been dragged into something terrible?{p}

They say the seven wonders handed down at this school come in dozens of versions, depending on who tells them.
Even for an old school, I'd thought that was far too many.
But if that was the case, I could understand it.
All those incidents had been Mr. Kuroki's doing{f:.|.}
Being told they were one connected chain of events felt more right than being told they were dozens of unrelated happenings.{p}

But...
{f:Wait a minute|Hold on}.
{f:I|I} realized something.{p}

When I looked, a crack had appeared in it.
What {f:timing|timing}.
It was as if the school were threatening {f:me|me}.{p}

Crack-crack!
The crack grew.
Fine cracks ran across the entire pane.
It was a wonder it didn't shatter to pieces{f:.|.}
The evening sun glinted off the glass, now white and opaque, in every direction.
For an instant, it made me think of a fierce stare that pinned me where I stood.{p}

"I see, so you want to hear it... Then maybe I'll tell you."
As Mr. Kuroki said that, his eyes seemed to flash darkly for an instant.
But before I could be sure, he spun around and turned his back to us.{p}

With a tremendous roar, the ground shook violently.
The ones inside the shelter were thrown every which way and sent tumbling.
Another bomb had hit the school building.{p}

Don't go blaming those people.
Like I said, it was a time when just keeping yourself alive was hard enough.
Then one night, some time after that, in the dead of night...{p}

From somewhere, a gleaming knife had appeared in the boy's hand.
"Stop!"
one of the grown-ups shouted.{p}

A while later, the war ended.
The time came for this school to serve its proper purpose again.
But... at the same time, a strange rumor began going around among the students.{p}

They said a boy's ghost appeared in the basement that used to be the food storeroom.
At first the teachers paid it no attention, but the students were so frightened that they decided to do something about it.
So they sealed the basement off.{p}

It was whispered right into my ear.
Startled, I tried to pull my ear away from the wall, when a second whisper came hard on its heels.
"I'll kill you."{p}

So actually, this is the first time I've seen this wall since then.
I thought it'd be scarier, but I'm surprisingly fine.
Well, I guess that just means I've grown up.{p}

...{f:We|We} left the school.
Honestly, that was just mean{f:|}.
Maybe it's in poor taste, but {f:I|I} was taking this project seriously.{p}

That scared me, and I ran away.
After that, I kept away from here.
The whole time, until I graduated.{p}

{f:We|We} put our ears to the wall.
Could there really be something to hear{f:?|?}
...I couldn't hear anything in particular.
That's strange{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} tried putting my other ear to the wall instead.{p}

Mr. Kuroki was still lying on the floor.
His face had gone past pale to white as paper.
I touched him.{p}

"...There's no pulse."
Mr. Kuroki was dead★
Had the girl's ghost done it{f:?|?}
Had I only imagined she was a harmless spirit who'd lost her brother{f:?|?}
Had she meant to drain his life force from the very start{f:?|?}
And yet {f:I|I} had been carelessly rejoicing at their reunion{f:.|.}
One wrong step, and it might have been {f:me|me} who died...{p}

But Mr. Kuroki burst out laughing.
"Scared you, did I? He's a friend of mine."
The flashlight beam lit up the figure.{p}

"Wh... Waaaagh!"
Hosoda brandished a box cutter he'd pulled out from who knows where.
He lunged at the man.{p}

But a split second before I could, the Reaper turned around.
The moment our eyes met, my body wouldn't move.
Mr. Kuroki let out a laugh.{p}

"Why, you★"
Mr. Kuroki noticed and lunged at me.
He was big and solidly built. I couldn't let him take the box cutter from me.{p}

{f:We|We} were saved...
Relieved, {f:I|I} went to help Hosoda up.
But my hand was knocked away.{p}

That's right.
After all, a lot of people died here.
It's no wonder their bitter regret would linger on.{p}

...{f:We|We} left the school.
Honestly, that was just mean{f:|}.
Maybe it's in poor taste, but {f:I|I} was taking this project seriously.{p}

I was standing in pitch darkness.
I could hear lots of voices moaning.
When I listened closely, they were saying the same thing I'd heard before.{p}

From the screaming mouth, flames came gushing out in a roaring whirl.
"Waaagh!"
With no time to dodge, Hosoda took the fire head-on.{p}

"Gyaaaaaah!"
Letting out a scream that didn't sound human, he rolled around on the floor.
He was a human torch from head to toe{f:|}.{p}

I tried to run to him, but the flames were too fierce to get close.
"Hosoda!"
As {f:I|I} screamed, Mr. Kuroki grabbed my shoulder.{p}

"Give me one too."
"Give us your body."
Saying things like that, one after another, the bloodied bodies came closer and closer.{p}

There was a click.
{f:Did it hang up?|So it hung up.}
{f:I|I} looked over at the phone.{p}

Then I saw that the receiver was off the hook.
{f:What?|Why?}
There was no one in this room but {f:me|me}.
Was I supposed to believe the receiver had come off by itself{f:?|?}
That was ridiculous.
{f:I|I} picked up the receiver.
Then, before I had even brought it to my ear, I heard a hoarse voice.{p}

"Death to whoever learns all seven wonders!
That is the law of old."
At the same moment, I heard something whistle through the air.{p}

Something was throbbing inside my head.
Was it the sound of blood pouring out of {f:my|my} body{f:?|?}
Everything before my eyes grew hazy.
I couldn't even think straight anymore.
Were Hosoda and the others all right{f:?|?}
Thinking about that, {f:I|I} collapsed into a pool of blood.
Maybe the seven wonders hid some far more important meaning.
But it was too late now.
{f:I|I} weakly closed my eyes.{p}

Having ranted at him without letting him get a word in, {f:I|I} hung up.
Maybe I had gone a little too far.
But I had just been through such a terrible ordeal today{f:.|.}
It was only natural to be a little on edge{f:.|.}{p}

But at some point, I {f:must have dozed off|dozed off}.
A flapping sound woke me up.
What{f:?|?}
The curtains were fluttering.
Had {f:I|I} forgotten to close the window{f:?|?}
As I tried to sit up, I realized someone was in my room.{p}

Taking a gamble, {f:I|I} flung my blanket at him.
It landed over Hosoda with a whump.
"Whoa★"
Now{f:!|!}
{f:I|I} slipped past him and tried to dash out of the room.{p}

Was he serious{f:?|?}
Would he be all right{f:?|?}
But {f:I|I} had told him I wasn't going.
Hosoda was on my mind, but {f:I|I} crawled into bed.
I really was tired{f:.|, after all.}
I wanted to get even a little sleep.{p}

"Access to the old school building is going to be a lot stricter from now on.
No one gets inside until the demolition starts."
That was what Mr. Kuroki said.
Maybe he regretted what happened yesterday, too.
This was the end of it{f:.|.}
The mysteries of the old school building would never be solved now{f:.|.}
I felt a little let down, but mostly I was relieved.
Life needs a bit of mystery{f:, but|, but} you have to be alive to enjoy anything{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} made a firm resolution not to poke into the seven wonders any further.{p}

I'd be lying if I said I wasn't curious.
{f:I|I} decided to just keep watching.
"Hyaaah-ha-ha-ha!"{p}

"You two!"
I thought we were going to get yelled at.
{f:But|But} when he turned around, his face had changed.
It was as if he was looking at someone else, not at {f:us|us}{f:.|.}
"You two were trying to let them out, weren't you?"
His voice was low and strangled.
He was like a different person from before{f:.|.}
"Th-them?"
"Don't play dumb! The ones squirming on the other side of this wall!
Those bloodthirsty things that rule this school from the shadows☆"{p}

I didn't understand what he was saying.
But if what he said was true, then all the scary stories I'd heard today were caused by something inside this wall{f:?|?}
...No, that couldn't be. That was just impossible.{p}

Half tumbling, we made it out to the schoolyard and headed for the gate.
We were almost there{f:.|.}
Just a little farther, and we should be back in the everyday world{f:.|.}
But then Hosoda tripped.
"Aaah!"
He fell flat on his face.
Right behind him, Mr. Kuroki closed in, the saw held high.
Was this it{f:★|★}
Just then, {f:we|we} were lit up by a dazzling light.{p}

"What's going on there★"
It was a police officer on patrol{f:.|!}
We were saved!{p}

The power saw switched on, and the motor's whine, like a woman's shriek, blew the silence apart.
"Hya-ha-ha!"
Hosoda raised it high and, without a moment's hesitation, cut into the wall.{p}

With a furious grinding, the wall crumbled away easily.
Without the slightest resistance, the wall laid its innards bare.
...It was too dark to see well.{p}

Ghostly faces that gave off no scent of life{f:.|.}
"Living humans..."
"Living humans..."
"Why are you alive?"
Bitter murmurs leaked out from all around.{p}

A chill ran through me, and my skin broke out in goosebumps.
Were they the students who had died{f:?|?}
Had {f:we|we} destroyed the wall that separated this world from them in the world beyond{f:?|?}{p}

The hand that had been gripping Hosoda slid back in.
Hosoda's big body swayed and toppled over.
"Hosoda!"
His skin had gone dry and papery.
He looked just like a mummy{f:.|.}
"Life force..."{p}

The power saw switched on, and the motor's whine, like a woman's shriek, blew the silence {f:apart|apart}.
"Hya-ha-ha!"
Hosoda raised it high and, without a moment's hesitation, cut into the wall.{p}

With a furious grinding, the wall crumbled away easily.
Without the slightest resistance, the wall laid its innards bare.
...It was too dark to see well.{p}

Suddenly, the racket stopped.
Hosoda was staring blankly into the hole.
Inside{f:,|,} there stood a lovely little girl{f:.|.}
Was she about elementary school age{f:?|?}
When I looked closer, her outline was blurring and melting into the darkness.
She {f:didn't seem|didn't seem} to be a living person.
But she didn't seem to mean any harm{f:.|.}
"What's {f:wrong|wrong}?"
"My big brother..."
The little ghost girl murmured.
{f:I|I} had an idea who she might be.
"She must be the little sister from Mr. Kuroki's story{f:.|.}
The one they said was carried in there."
"I see."
Hosoda nodded.{p}

"Did you get separated from your brother's spirit? Poor thing."
As he said it, he held out his hand to her.
"Come on out. I'll help you look for him."{p}

The power saw switched on, and the motor's whine, like a woman's shriek, blew the silence {f:apart|apart}.
"Hya-ha-ha!"
Hosoda raised it high and, without a moment's hesitation, cut into the wall.{p}

With a furious grinding, the wall crumbled away easily.
Without the slightest resistance, the wall laid its innards bare.
...It was too dark to see well.{p}

"Graaaaagh☆"
{f:I|I} tried to dodge, but tripped over the power saw, which was still running.
VRRRANG!{p}
